Z||000009||LZeitgeist||08-10-2001||09:38 AM||||Damn, the idiots didn't even redesign the correct item... they redesigned a pushpin, not a thumbtack.<P>A thumbtack is a small round metal disk with a pin protruding from the center of one side, and it is used by pushing the item into the surface with one's thumb, since it is not usable while holding it with a thumb and a finger, hence the name 'thumbtack'. <P>A pushpin is utilized by holding it between thumb and fingers and pushing it into the surface, hence the name 'pushpin'. <P>Damn, if they're going to win a medal for redesigning the thumbtack, they could at least have started with the correct object in the first place. 'Design students' my butt.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Steve Normington||08-10-2001||03:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>A thumbtack is a small round metal disk with a pin protruding from the center of one side, and it is used by pushing the item into the surface with one's thumb, since it is not usable while holding it with a thumb and a finger, hence the name 'thumbtack'. <P>A pushpin is utilized by holding it between thumb and fingers and pushing it into the surface, hence the name 'pushpin'. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Maybe they added a easy to hold grip to the thumbtack.||||reg||1
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||08-10-2001||03:43 PM||||And by doing so, they created the pushpin.||||reg||1
