Z||000015||Ken Wittlief||08-11-2001||10:27 AM||||In practical use Id be surprized if these will be usefull for much of anything on a cork board or bulletin board. <P> Ive found for hanging a frame on a cubical wall a paper clip unfolded into an S shape hooks the frame and hookd the fabric pretty well - but why would you want to hang a picture frame on a bulletin board?!<P> and if you tried to I dont think these would stay stuck in <P>  I dont have a need to put wires on a bulletin board.<P>  I think these kids have fallen into the 'build a better mouse trap and the world will beat a path to your door' fallicy.<P>  the error in this is: we dont have a mouse problem in the first place.<P>  and we dont have a 'attach wires and frames to bulletin boards' problem either.||||reg||11
Z||000016||FieroHeather||08-11-2001||09:03 PM||||I was thinking the same thing Ken, when I read the article<P>--"pushpins" dont hold much weight...so why would I want to 'hang' something off of them in the first place?  They would rip right out of the wall!<P>Look where the center of gravity of a "pushpin" is.  If the thread/string were to be moved the furthest forward, the weight would shift, and it would come out of the wall.<P>People need to be spending their time on something else useful, like inventing ways to maximize the land for feeding the human population.  *sheesh*||||reg||1
