Z||000019||Ken Wittlief||08-13-2001||10:49 AM||||actaully songman is not too far off - the problems with feeding the hungry right now isnt that we have a shortage of food<P> the problem is getting the food to the people that need it<P> sometimes its a logistics problem - it costs more to move the food than the food costs itself - an engineering/transportation problem<P>  sometimes its a political problem - the leaders of some countries seem to want to let their undesirable people starve.<P> but Heather is right - its better to take an existing problem and find a solution for it, that to try to come up with some clever new invention, and then try and figure out what to do with it.||||reg||1
